---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"Device Interface | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"Cassini Fixtures are a rugged modular device interface that extends the application range from DC to 120 GHz as a rapid changeout system for production.\n    Fixtures extend and enhance the instrument capabilities with an integrated calibration layer that guarantees signal accuracy to the device pin. "}
  active={["nav-products"]}>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
    <section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Device Interface</h2>
        <ol class="breadcrumb">
          <li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/products.html">Products</a></li>
          <li class="active">Device Interface</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->
    <script is:inline>
      $(document).ready(function () {
        $('#FixImg').ImageMapResize({
          origImageWidth: "705"
        });
      });
    </script>
    <style is:inline>
      .flexCenter {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        margin: 10% 0;
        min-height: 200px;
      }

      #nextPages div.col-sm-4 {
        text-align: center;
        padding: 20px 20px;
      }

      #nextPages h3 {
        text-align: center;
      }

      #nextPages p {
        text-align: left;
        padding: 20px 45px;
      }
    </style>

    <section id="primary">
      <div id="content" class="roosC container">
        <div class="row">
          <h1>Architect the Best Production Test</h1>
          <p class="main col-md-10">
            Fixtures carry the modular architecture of Cassini into the device interface environment. Housed in a rugged
            aluminum enclosure is a completely configurable test resource environment. It provides a versatile
            application range from DC to 90GHz and a rapid changeout system in production. Seamless integration with
            Cassini’s
            software allow fixtures to extend and enhance the capabilities of test instruments with an integrated
            calibration layer that guarantees signal accuracy right to the device pin. </p>
          <img class="centerImg" style="max-width: 1200px" title="Fixture Cost Layers" alt="Fixture Cost Layers"
            src="images/fix1.png">
        </div>
        <hr class="space">
        <div class="row">
          <h2>Flip the Cost Model</h2>
          <p class="main">
            All of the functionality and capability of traditional load boards have been re-engineered to take advantage
            of the configurable instrument framework of Cassini. Separating the device interface into two layers enables
            maximum design flexibility for high performance measurements that can adapt to changing application needs
            cost
            effectively. </p>
          <img class="centerImg" style="max-width: 1200px" title="Fixture Cost Model Advantages"
            alt="Fixture Cost Model Advantages" src="images/fix2.png">
        </div>
        <hr class="space">
        <div>
          <h2>Accuracy at the Device</h2>
          <p class="main">
            Cassini’s software manages the calibration layers automatically. As fixtures and device
            interface boards are interchanged with the test system, each calibration layer is cascaded to extend the
            calibrated measurement plane for port match and signal loss correction. This guarantees an accurate and
            repeatable test setup on the production floor for any device application.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-5 col-md-offset-1">
              <img class="centerImg" title="System Calibration Layers" alt="System Calibration Layers"
                src="images/fix10.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-5">
              <img class="centerImg" title="System Block Diagram" alt="System Block Diagram" src="images/fix11.png">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <hr class="space">
        <div class="row">
          <h2>Configurable Resource Mapping</h2>
          <p class="main">
            With the ability to configure and reconfigure the device interface, Cassini’s software helps manage all of
            complexity. You define serialized signal paths, resource switch controls, and additional
            measurement resources and the system automatically links calibrated paths together.</p>
          <img class="centerImg" title="Cassini 16 Fixture" alt="Cassini Fixture" src="images/fix9.png"
            style="max-width: 900px">
        </div>
        <hr class="space">
        <hr style="height: 3px; background: #0849a1;">
        <hr class="space">
        <div class="row">
          <h2>Taking Modular to a Whole New Level</h2>
          <p class="main">
            A modular test system is only as modular as it's least configurable component. All of the functionality and
            capability of traditional load boards have been re-engineered to take advantage of the configurable
            instrument framework of Cassini. The discrete layers enable maximum design flexibility for high performance
            RF devices that can adapt to changing application needs.
          </p>
          <img id="FixImg" class="centerImg" style="max-width: 705px" title="Cassini Modular Fixture Layers"
            alt="Cassini Modular Fixture Layers" usemap="#image-map" src="images/fix3.png">
          <map name="image-map">
            <area target="" alt="System Integration Layer" title="System Integration Layer" href="#Fix1"
              coords="0,720,705,921" shape="rect">
            <area target="" alt="Production Test Bench" title="Production Test Bench" href="#Fix2"
              coords="0,720,705,260" shape="rect">
            <area target="" alt="Launch Precision Measurement" title="Launch Precision Measurement" href="#Fix3"
              coords="0,109,705,260" shape="rect">
            <area target="" alt="High Frequency Performance" title="High Frequency Performance" href="#Fix4"
              coords="0,0,705,109" shape="rect">
          </map>
        </div>
        <div>
          <hr class="space">
          <hr>
          <hr class="space">
          <div class="row">
            <a id="Fix1" class="anchor"></a>
            <div class="col-sm-6">
              <img alt="System Integration Layer" src="images/fix4.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-offset-1 col-md-offset-0 col-sm-6" style="padding-top: 50px;">
              <img src="images/1.svg" title="#1" style="width:25px;">
              <h2>Multi‑Instrument Test Done Right</h2>
              <p class="main">
                A truly unique aspect of Cassini ATE is the RF system integration layer in the device interface. The 16
                universal instruments slots accommodate interchangeable interface blocks and interconnect, allowing the
                test system’s architecture to be dynamically configured for each device application. </p>
              <a href="products.html">Learn More &raquo;</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <hr class="space">

          <div class="row">
            <a id="Fix2" class="anchor"></a>
            <div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-push-6">
              <img title=" Cassini 16 Fixture" alt="Cassini Fixture" src="images/fix5.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-pull-6">
              <img src="images/2.svg" title="#2" style="width:25px;">
              <h2>Production Test Bench</h2>
              <p class="main">
                Fixtures enable easy access to microwave components while protecting them in a ruggedized, RF-shielded
                enclosure during production. It also supports expandable instrument capability with fixture module cards
                such as driver control for electromechanical relays and microwave switches as well as signal
                attenuation, amplification, and additional parametric measure resources.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <hr class="space">
          <div class="row">
            <a id="Fix3" class="anchor"></a>
            <div class="col-sm-6">
              <img alt="Fixture Layers" src="images/fix6.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-6">
              <img src="images/3.svg" title="#3" style="width:25px;">
              <h2>Launch Precision Measurement</h2>
              <p class="main">
                Interchangeable DC, high-speed digital, and microwave inserts provide precise contact signal launches
                onto the device interface board.The inserts support a flexible signal topology for customizing to
                applications and creating symmetric multi-site layouts. </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">
          <a id="Fix4" class="anchor"></a>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3 col-sm-push-6" style="padding-right: 0;">
              <img class="centerImg" alt="Quick-Lock1" src="images/fix7.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-3 col-sm-push-6" style="padding-left: 0;">
              <img class="centerImg" alt="Quick-Lock1" src="images/fix8.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-pull-6">
              <img src="images/4.svg" title="#4" style="width:25px;">
              <h2>High Frequency Performance</h2>
              <p class="main">
                The two-layer PCB and aluminum reinforcement combine high frequency performance and production
                durability. The design simplifies board layout, reduces the cost of high wear components, and enables
                quick changeout in production.
                <span class="pull-right"><a href="/dibs.html" class="link pull-right">Learn About the DIB
                    &raquo;</a></span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <hr class="space">
          <hr style="height: 3px; background: #0849a1;">
          <hr class="space">
          <div id="nextPages">
            <h2>Software Integration</h2>
            <div class="row hidden-xs hidden-sm">
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <a class="link" href="/guru.html" title="Guru Synergy"><i class="fa fa-puzzle-piece fa-5x"
                    aria-hidden="true" style="margin: auto;  width: 50%;"></i></a>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <a class="link" href="/guru.html" title="Guru Traceability"><i class='fas fa-fingerprint fa-4x'></i></a>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <a class="link" href="/guru.html" title="Guru Workflow"><i class="fa-solid fa-sitemap fa-3x"></i></a>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <h3>Synergy</h3>
                <p>
                  Deep integration with Cassini’s instrument software, system configuration management, and calibration
                  scheme, makes the device interface an extension of the tester.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <h3>Traceability</h3>
                <p>Guru enterprise provides back-end database support for automated updates, auto-loading calibration,
                  and resource tracking to support production logistics anywhere in the world.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="col-sm-4" style="text-align: center; padding: 20px 20px;">
                <h3>Workflow</h3>
                <p>Native software support provides access to the latest features and updates for a powerful and
                  efficient workflow from device characterization to high volume test.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="pull-right"><a href="/software.html" class="link pull-right">Learn More about Software
              &raquo;</a></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</Base>
